<p><img src="https://cdn3.brettterpstra.com/uploads/2026/07/marked-ql-header-rb.7532.jpg" width="800" height="226" style="margin:0 auto;clear:both;" class="header" /></p>
<p><a href="https://markedapp.com/ql">Marked QL</a>, my new Markdown Quick Look previewer, has met a warm reception, and I wanted to update everyone on a couple of things.</p>

<h3 id="on-the-price">On the price</h3>

<p>First off, yes, I increased the price of Marked QL from $4.99 to $9.99. I did this in anticipation of a new version of Marked QL that will increase its functionality, but then my update got rejected by Apple. I decided to leave the price there and see how it does, and hope that the update will be out in the next couple of days.</p>

<p>The goal of the price increase would be to have less customer support and more invested customers. It will likely mean a drop in sales, but fewer support requests while I work through the initial releases. It&rsquo;s an experiment. I still haven&rsquo;t raised the price of <a href="https://markedapp.com">Marked 3</a> from its &ldquo;intro&rdquo; price, and I&rsquo;ll offer a little more notice if/when that time comes.</p>

<h3 id="support-issues">Support issues</h3>

<p>The biggest issue that I&rsquo;ve seen is that I originally only read the UTIs <code class="language-plaintext highlighter-rouge">net.daringfireball.markdown</code> and <code class="language-plaintext highlighter-rouge">public.text</code>. Unfortunately (for me, especially), a bunch of apps write their own custom UTIs for Markdown files, such as <code class="language-plaintext highlighter-rouge">net.ia.markdown</code> if you&rsquo;ve run iA Writer, or worse <code class="language-plaintext highlighter-rouge">unknown.markdown</code> if you&rsquo;ve ever run TeXShop. I&rsquo;ve added as many of these UTIs as I can for the next update. I was really hoping that update would be out by now, as the bug is causing more refunds than I would like.</p>

<p>Marked QL really does work with any Markdown file, but on a lot of systems Markdown files get &ldquo;owned&rdquo; by apps that change the <abbr title="Universal Type Identifier">UTI</abbr>.</p>

<h3 id="whats-next">What&rsquo;s next</h3>

<p>The next version of Marked QL (submitted for review) will add dark mode, Table of Contents navigation, (limited) Quarto processing based on the latest updates to Apex, and will solve a host of issues like those mentioned above. The nice thing about Marked QL being based on Apex is that I&rsquo;m getting a lot of feedback on <a href="https://apexmarkdown.org">Apex</a> itself, which in turn improves the open source technology behind Marked QL.</p>

<p>The next update after that will add font size support from config and a few other new features. That update is still in progress.</p>

<p>I&rsquo;m hoping to turn Marked QL users into Marked 3 users, but Apple won&rsquo;t let me include the &ldquo;Get Marked 3&rdquo; button I had there initially, so I&rsquo;ve been relegated to just having a Help menu item for it. That&rsquo;s fine, I don&rsquo;t care. It&rsquo;s not against the rules to have a link, but it&rsquo;s against the rules to use the <code class="language-plaintext highlighter-rouge">lsopen</code> command I was using to either open in Marked 3 or link to get it.</p>

<h3 id="share-and-get-a-free-copy">Share and get a free copy</h3>

<p>I&rsquo;d appreciate help getting the word out about Marked QL (and Marked 3) for that matter. So if you say something nice and link to <a href="https://markedapp.com/ql">https://markedapp.com/ql</a> on X and tag @markedapp, or post on Mastodon and tag @marked@indieapps.space, I&rsquo;ll enter you in a drawing for a free copy of Marked QL (which you can give to a friend if you already own it).</p>

<p>If you want to share about it on your blog and would like a review copy, just <a href="https://brettterpstra.com/contact/">contact me</a></p>

<p>If you share about it on other social media, send me a link and I&rsquo;ll enter you as well! I have plenty of copies to give away, so you have a decent chance of scoring one.</p>

<p>Check out Marked QL at <a href="https://markedapp.com/ql">markedapp.com/ql</a>.</p>

